# EAS Build uploads the git root of the monorepo, and it reads .easignore only here, at the root
# (eas-cli: Ignore(rootDir) with rootDir = git top level). When .easignore exists EAS does not
# read any .gitignore, so this file repeats the relevant rules of app/.gitignore on purpose.
# Only app/ is needed for a native build; everything else stays on this machine.
# Local env files never leave this machine: build values come only from the profile env in
# app/eas.json (production and preview set every EXPO_PUBLIC_WARDENCLAW_* explicitly to "unset"
# or "0", bench only adds EXPO_PUBLIC_WARDENCLAW_BENCH=1). Personal dev values live in app/.env.local.
app/.env
app/.env.*
!app/.env.example
/daemon/
/plugin/
/site/
/protocol/
/docs/
/.github/

node_modules/
.DS_Store
*.log
*.jks
*.p8
*.p12
*.key
*.mobileprovision
app/.expo/
app/dist/
app/web-build/
app/*.orig.*
app/.test-build/
app/.test-build-e2e/
app/build/
# Generated by `expo prebuild` in a local build: if they were uploaded, EAS would treat the
# project as bare and skip prebuild. Keep the app managed (CNG).
app/ios/
app/android/
